WEBVTT

00:00.270 --> 00:07.150
The new morning we've finally found

00:00.270 --> 00:07.150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

00:07.150 --> 00:11.190
is being hampered by the past.

00:07.150 --> 00:11.190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

00:11.390 --> 00:16.660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

00:11.390 --> 00:16.660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

00:16.660 --> 00:20.490
but the past so full of remorse.

00:16.660 --> 00:20.490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

00:21.870 --> 00:26.960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

00:21.870 --> 00:26.960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

00:26.960 --> 00:31.050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

00:26.960 --> 00:31.050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

00:32.340 --> 00:36.890
It's about now that a teardrop

00:32.340 --> 00:36.890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

00:36.890 --> 00:41.560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

00:36.890 --> 00:41.560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

00:41.890 --> 00:46.810
Will this rain ever stop?

00:41.890 --> 00:46.810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

00:46.810 --> 00:52.030
I've been freezing for a long time.

00:46.810 --> 00:52.030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

00:52.030 --> 00:57.320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

00:52.030 --> 00:57.320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

00:57.320 --> 01:02.080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

00:57.320 --> 01:02.080
Tsutsumarete iikana

01:02.080 --> 01:06.870
Today, the rain falls again;

01:02.080 --> 01:06.870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

01:06.870 --> 01:12.090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

01:06.870 --> 01:12.090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

01:12.090 --> 01:17.130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

01:12.090 --> 01:17.130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

01:17.680 --> 01:28.850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

01:17.680 --> 01:28.850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

01:30.000 --> 01:33.000
The Immortal Legion

01:30.000 --> 01:33.000
The Immortal Legion

01:54.010 --> 01:56.010
It hurts...

01:54.920 --> 01:56.760
Help me...

01:56.800 --> 01:58.760
I'm starving!

01:59.720 --> 02:00.930
Water...!

02:00.930 --> 02:02.100
It hurts!

02:02.390 --> 02:05.600
"Not yet finished experimenting"?

02:05.600 --> 02:07.390
This in itself is the experiment!

02:07.390 --> 02:08.850
It was a success!

02:09.190 --> 02:15.360
The ultimate soldiers that never die, betray, and always fight according to our orders.

02:15.360 --> 02:19.110
An immortal army has been created!

02:20.410 --> 02:21.950
Pa...pa?

02:23.080 --> 02:24.290
That's right!

02:24.580 --> 02:26.830
I am your father!

02:26.830 --> 02:30.210
Now, listen closely to what I'm about to say.

02:30.210 --> 02:35.130
Currently, there are several rebels targeting these headquarters!

02:35.130 --> 02:36.670
Papa!

02:37.010 --> 02:38.340
You all are to-

03:06.410 --> 03:07.660
Ouch...

03:08.580 --> 03:09.710
That hurts.

03:09.710 --> 03:10.790
That hurts!

03:10.210 --> 03:11.420
Pain!

03:11.420 --> 03:12.540
That hurts...

03:12.540 --> 03:14.250
Ouch...

03:14.250 --> 03:15.380
It hurts...

03:15.380 --> 03:16.420
The pain...

03:28.890 --> 03:30.980
What a huge gate.

03:30.980 --> 03:33.350
I don't like the feeling it gives off.

03:33.350 --> 03:35.150
Is this really the place?

03:35.150 --> 03:35.940
Yeah.

03:36.650 --> 03:38.400
It looks exactly as Al described it.

03:39.940 --> 03:41.650
Who the heck is that?

03:42.320 --> 03:44.280
Number 66.

03:44.280 --> 03:45.910
Barry the Chopper.

03:46.620 --> 03:48.740
He was Slicer's partner.

04:05.970 --> 04:09.010
Open...!

04:11.060 --> 04:12.690
Dammit...!

04:12.690 --> 04:14.730
How the hell are we supposed to open this?!

04:17.820 --> 04:18.770
Step aside.

04:25.360 --> 04:26.200
It opened-

04:40.340 --> 04:45.300
Order the soldiers from Central that are fighting with the Briggs forces and Mustang to retreat.

04:50.220 --> 04:52.430
Oh? Are you going to shoot?

04:56.650 --> 04:58.940
Looks like your men aren't very disciplined.

05:03.780 --> 05:05.650
If you don't hurry up and have them retreat,

05:05.650 --> 05:08.570
the soldiers from Briggs will continue to fight with no mercy.

05:09.120 --> 05:12.200
Wouldn't it bother you if you lost every single one of your soldiers?

05:25.130 --> 05:28.890
Shut the northern, southern, eastern, and western gates that allow entry into the Central Headquarters!

05:29.180 --> 05:34.060
Don't let a single enemy force from Briggs or Mustang's party enter!

05:35.980 --> 05:39.060
So you're rotten, but it looks like you've still retained a set of testicles.

05:39.060 --> 05:41.070
Don't get too cocky, bitch!

05:41.070 --> 05:45.240
I'll have all of you monkeys from Briggs crushed-

05:55.000 --> 05:56.040
Huh?

05:57.000 --> 05:59.710
Oh, this one.

06:01.130 --> 06:03.590
You're not supposed to interfere.

06:04.420 --> 06:08.050
I was told to defeat you.

06:09.090 --> 06:10.890
What a drag...

06:12.180 --> 06:14.470
You've just created another spot for me at the top.

06:14.850 --> 06:17.640
I thank you, Homunculus!

06:17.770 --> 06:24.440
You've saved me from having to stain this celebrated sword passed down in my family for generations!

06:33.700 --> 06:34.740
You-

06:48.260 --> 06:49.550
They won't die?!

06:51.390 --> 06:52.890
It hurts...

06:55.680 --> 06:58.350
I'm starving!

06:58.640 --> 06:59.890
It hurts!

06:59.230 --> 07:01.100
The pain!

07:01.190 --> 07:05.150
Brother!

07:05.150 --> 07:06.400
Don't tell me...!

07:10.110 --> 07:12.910
Did they attach souls to dolls?!

07:12.910 --> 07:15.200
Dammit! There's no end to them!

07:15.700 --> 07:17.240
What the hell are these things?!

07:17.240 --> 07:18.330
Hell if I know!

07:18.330 --> 07:20.410
Why aren't they dying?!

07:20.920 --> 07:22.420
This is bad.

07:22.420 --> 07:24.710
If we were to let them outside...!

07:31.090 --> 07:32.640
Did something happen?

07:32.640 --> 07:33.760
No idea.

07:33.970 --> 07:37.140
I heard Colonel Mustang pulled a coup d'etat.

07:37.430 --> 07:39.310
How frightening.

07:39.310 --> 07:41.350
There, there. Don't cry.

07:45.150 --> 07:46.230
What do we do...

07:48.400 --> 07:49.780
You-

07:51.950 --> 07:53.780
Oh no! They're getting out!

08:03.830 --> 08:06.750
My bad, I sealed off the exit.

08:06.750 --> 08:08.210
Don't worry about it.

08:08.210 --> 08:11.300
If you hadn't done it, I would have destroyed the exit myself.

08:11.300 --> 08:13.970
Now we can prepare for the worst!

08:14.090 --> 08:18.390
Okay, so now that we don't have to worry about them getting out...

08:18.390 --> 08:21.270
...let's show them what we've got!

08:25.690 --> 08:27.190
It hurts!

08:27.560 --> 08:29.570
So much pain!

08:31.320 --> 08:33.780
How dare they make something like this...!

08:34.240 --> 08:38.780
Guess we have to go through these guys first to give the old guy a beatdown.

08:42.080 --> 08:44.870
This is gonna be rough!

08:48.210 --> 08:51.090
Mustang is currently escaping in an ice cream truck!

08:51.090 --> 08:52.590
Barricade the main roads!

08:53.130 --> 08:56.760
The truck may look normal,
but it's filled with weapons and ammo!

08:56.760 --> 08:57.970
Don't let your guard down!

09:06.310 --> 09:07.770
A-A bear!

09:07.770 --> 09:09.980
A bear with a mohawk!

09:13.650 --> 09:14.780
Signal lost.

09:14.780 --> 09:18.030
A bear with a mohawk...?

09:18.030 --> 09:20.330
Captain Buccaneer from the Northern Army.

09:20.950 --> 09:24.250
Colonel, it seems like it'll be difficult to enter the city.

09:25.790 --> 09:27.420
Yeah.

09:31.920 --> 09:34.550
An ice cream truck, huh...?

09:38.260 --> 09:41.260
I wonder if they're doing well.

09:44.600 --> 09:48.350
But it's irritating that I can't fight alongside them.

09:48.350 --> 09:52.070
I never knew how annoying it can be to wait.

09:56.280 --> 09:58.950
I've been hearing this sound since yesterday.

09:59.490 --> 10:01.950
Hey Alphonse, what is that sound?

10:02.240 --> 10:05.250
Selim's playing with my head.

10:11.540 --> 10:15.130
He may be a monster on the inside, but I guess he's still a brat.

10:24.310 --> 10:25.930
Make him stop, Alphonse!

10:27.020 --> 10:29.140
Make him stop those noises!

10:29.140 --> 10:30.350
It's morse code!

10:30.350 --> 10:32.190
Signals the army uses for communication!

10:39.280 --> 10:41.530
He's telling someone our current location-

11:03.510 --> 11:04.300
Hi.

11:04.930 --> 11:08.600
Thanks for coming to pick me up, Kimblee.

11:10.060 --> 11:14.480
Seriously... please stop giving me extra work.

11:16.150 --> 11:18.280
Come on, give me a break.

11:18.860 --> 11:20.780
I won't let my guard down again.

11:42.260 --> 11:44.010
W-What are these things?!

11:44.010 --> 11:45.800
You tricked me, Envy!

11:45.970 --> 11:48.810
D-Did not!

11:49.140 --> 11:50.810
Immortality is just beyond-

11:50.850 --> 11:51.810
Oww!

11:51.980 --> 11:54.350
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

12:06.280 --> 12:08.120
You bitch!!

12:26.550 --> 12:28.390
Yes!!

13:10.970 --> 13:13.100
Guess who's back?!

13:24.780 --> 13:30.990
Thanks for bringing me here, little brat.

13:37.580 --> 13:39.960
Why are there soldiers here?

13:39.960 --> 13:41.670
Are they here to make us leave?

13:42.000 --> 13:45.630
Oh no... there's nowhere else to go.

13:46.510 --> 13:48.300
W-What's this all about?

13:48.300 --> 13:51.640
Don't tell me they've found out where we're hiding...

13:51.640 --> 13:54.100
Oh no, Alphonse!

13:54.100 --> 13:55.730
Hang on, Doctor!

13:56.020 --> 13:59.560
What if they found out you're Doctor Marcoh?!

13:59.560 --> 14:02.900
But I can't just sit back and watch...

14:04.320 --> 14:05.860
Take a moment to calm down.

14:06.110 --> 14:11.070
If you were to be taken hostage,
it would only hurt Alphonse and the others.

14:12.280 --> 14:14.370
It's dangerous to just move around without thinking.

14:14.370 --> 14:15.790
Let's stay put.

14:15.790 --> 14:16.960
Yeah? Yeah?

14:32.140 --> 14:33.720
Are you alone?

14:34.140 --> 14:36.770
I heard that Gluttony was here with you.

14:37.230 --> 14:40.230
I made use of him.

14:40.230 --> 14:41.690
You ate him?

14:41.980 --> 14:43.150
Your own comrade?

14:44.020 --> 14:47.570
Not a comrade. We're part of the same being.

14:48.360 --> 14:51.030
We were born from the same father.

14:51.780 --> 14:54.620
Think of it as "coming back together", per se.

14:54.620 --> 14:56.580
I see.

14:58.330 --> 14:59.540
Mr. Heinkel!

15:05.840 --> 15:08.130
Wow, you're still alive?

15:08.590 --> 15:12.550
Can't underestimate a chimera's survival power, after all.

15:13.800 --> 15:14.970
Mr. Heinkel!

15:18.180 --> 15:19.180
Dammit!

15:20.560 --> 15:21.810
Let go!

15:22.440 --> 15:23.810
I won't let you get away.

15:24.110 --> 15:25.520
You-

15:35.080 --> 15:36.620
Don't know when to give up, do you.

15:52.800 --> 15:54.300
Stop running away.

16:05.610 --> 16:06.860
What?

16:08.530 --> 16:09.860
I knew it wouldn't work.

16:10.400 --> 16:13.360
That's as far as you're going to get,
Major General Armstrong!

16:14.910 --> 16:18.870
A shoot-on-sight order has been issued for your treason!

16:21.080 --> 16:22.160
Ready!

16:23.040 --> 16:24.210
Fire!

16:26.250 --> 16:27.210
Idiot.

16:27.790 --> 16:30.210
Placing your men in this situation is just foolish.

16:46.230 --> 16:48.940
Here's to hoping that did some damage to you...

16:51.530 --> 16:53.780
I've got you now.

16:56.200 --> 16:59.740
Didn't get the wrong one this time.

17:03.540 --> 17:05.710
Female general...

17:06.170 --> 17:07.420
...must die.

17:18.550 --> 17:21.520
Sister!!

17:21.520 --> 17:25.060
Are you all right?!

17:27.650 --> 17:30.820
Who are you even talking to, Alex?!

17:31.190 --> 17:33.740
Glad to see you're safe.

17:33.740 --> 17:37.160
And so, what is that thing?

17:37.910 --> 17:39.490
A Homunculus.

17:39.490 --> 17:41.870
A bullet isn't enough to even move him an inch.

17:43.080 --> 17:45.410
Maybe a little budge with a cannon.

17:45.410 --> 17:46.670
Oh, my!

17:47.540 --> 17:50.790
This is my specialty!

17:52.050 --> 17:57.430
Please let your brother, Alex, handle this!

17:57.760 --> 18:00.300
Come, monster!

18:02.510 --> 18:05.680
Such a drag...

18:14.320 --> 18:16.530
Don't mind me...

18:17.990 --> 18:20.280
Hurry up... and escape...

18:20.280 --> 18:21.370
No!

18:21.370 --> 18:23.200
Don't be stupid.

18:23.200 --> 18:25.540
At this rate, neither of us will make it.

18:26.500 --> 18:30.960
If you leave me behind, at least you may be able to survive.

18:30.960 --> 18:32.670
I said, no!

18:33.380 --> 18:37.420
Focus on living for now!

18:37.420 --> 18:38.720
Idiot!

18:39.680 --> 18:41.180
Take a good look at reality.

18:41.180 --> 18:44.140
We're put against Kimblee and Pride.

18:47.600 --> 18:50.020
Just leave me behind...!

18:51.100 --> 18:52.900
Don't give up!

18:52.900 --> 18:54.860
I'll save you for sure!

18:59.240 --> 19:00.950
Dammit...!

19:00.950 --> 19:03.700
Move, stupid leg!

19:03.700 --> 19:10.250
We can't lose here!

19:12.330 --> 19:14.500
Mr. Heinkel, hang onto me!

19:14.500 --> 19:16.590
Don't you dare give up!

19:16.590 --> 19:19.670
You siblings are so...

19:21.010 --> 19:26.680
Why do you try to save others
when you're all damaged as well?

19:29.640 --> 19:31.270
I made a promise.

19:32.230 --> 19:34.110
I made a promise with Brother,

19:34.900 --> 19:38.400
that we won't let anyone die again.

19:44.870 --> 19:46.660
You're right.

19:47.200 --> 19:51.290
I recall even Kimblee saying that "if you survive, you win."

19:53.540 --> 19:57.170
Thanks to that, I remembered that I had something good with me.

20:03.010 --> 20:05.180
Why do you have this?

20:05.930 --> 20:10.930
I picked it up at the mines to the north after being abandoned by Kimblee...

20:12.060 --> 20:13.560
A philosopher's stone...

20:14.480 --> 20:17.270
We really may be able to beat them if we have this.

20:17.940 --> 20:18.820
But still!

20:18.820 --> 20:20.860
Yeah, I know.

20:21.280 --> 20:23.990
This is made of human lives, right?

20:25.780 --> 20:32.040
I've heard from your brother that you guys don't want to use this to return to your bodies.

20:32.750 --> 20:34.000
In that case...

20:34.920 --> 20:40.550
In that case, use them to save the world; not for yourselves.

20:42.090 --> 20:44.510
I'm asking you because you're willing to acknowledge them as human lives,

20:44.630 --> 20:48.510
even after being reduced to such a state.

20:49.510 --> 20:51.980
I can understand their feelings.

20:53.940 --> 21:00.020
No matter what they may look like now, they still want to fight to protect what's precious to them.

21:01.110 --> 21:04.450
Give them a chance to fight too.

21:11.450 --> 21:12.620
Okay.

21:13.870 --> 21:15.620
Give them a good beatdown,

21:17.130 --> 21:18.590
Alphonse.

21:18.960 --> 21:19.840
Yeah.

21:22.260 --> 21:24.720
Let's fight them together.

21:27.590 --> 21:30.310
This cloud of dust is annoying.

21:30.310 --> 21:33.220
Should I blow it away with an explosion?

21:33.220 --> 21:34.100
No,

21:34.390 --> 21:37.980
they're both still inside it.

21:37.980 --> 21:39.980
Besides, he won't be able to escape without his legs-

21:59.380 --> 22:01.380
Oh, my.

22:01.380 --> 22:03.050
Instead of escaping, you...

22:12.680 --> 22:13.770
Marvelous.

22:15.890 --> 22:20.980
Very entertaining, Alphonse Elric!

22:27.950 --> 22:31.500
Ever since that day passed,

22:27.950 --> 22:31.500
Ano hi kara zutto

22:31.500 --> 22:35.750
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

22:31.500 --> 22:35.750
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

22:36.290 --> 22:41.300
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

22:36.290 --> 22:41.300
Itami wo kasanetemo

22:41.300 --> 22:46.410
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

22:41.300 --> 22:46.410
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

22:47.890 --> 22:49.850
I'll never be able

22:47.890 --> 22:49.850
Mou modorenai

22:49.850 --> 22:52.350
to return to those days.

22:49.850 --> 22:52.350
Ikutsumo no hibi

22:52.350 --> 22:57.440
I'm still powerless.

22:52.350 --> 22:57.440
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

22:57.440 --> 23:02.690
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

22:57.440 --> 23:02.690
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

23:02.690 --> 23:08.560
memories of when you were still with me.

23:02.690 --> 23:08.560
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

23:09.240 --> 23:11.580
I long to become

23:09.240 --> 23:11.580
Kyou yori motto

23:11.580 --> 23:14.330
stronger than I am now,

23:11.580 --> 23:14.330
Tsuyoku naritai

23:14.330 --> 23:19.470
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

23:14.330 --> 23:19.470
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

23:19.470 --> 23:21.840
If the wind happens to stop

23:19.470 --> 23:21.840
Arukitsuzukete

23:21.840 --> 23:24.550
in the midst of my long journey,

23:21.840 --> 23:24.550
Kaze ga yandara

23:24.550 --> 23:29.260
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

23:24.550 --> 23:29.260
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

23:30.010 --> 23:36.600
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

23:30.010 --> 23:36.600
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

23:37.770 --> 23:42.150
A rainbow spans across the sky.

23:37.770 --> 23:42.150
Niji ga kakaruyo

23:58.870 --> 24:04.540
If it's a fight between man and man, choose the path you believe is right.

24:05.210 --> 24:10.840
Only a fool would stand indecisive after being frightened at the thought of being soiled by the mud.

24:12.300 --> 24:16.300
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

24:16.300 --> 24:20.830
Episode 52, Combined Strength.

24:16.330 --> 24:20.830
Combined Strength

24:21.620 --> 24:25.170
It is beyond the point of hesitation.
